1. Source ROS and the workspace

2. Build the package

3. Launch the robot model in RViz
This opens the URDF visualization without Gazebo:


The file used for this launch is display.launch.py.

4. Launch the Gazebo simulation
This starts the simulated vehicle in Gazebo and connects the ROS-Gazebo bridge:


The launch entry point is gz_sim_launch.py.

5. Enable keyboard teleoperation
If you want to drive the robot manually:


6. Main robot topics
The robot publishes and consumes these core ROS topics:

/cmd_vel — command input for steering and motion
/joint_states — wheel and steering positions
/tf and /tf_static — robot transforms
/lidar_scan — LiDAR sensor data
/imu/data — IMU readings
/front_camera/image_raw, /right_camera/image_raw, /rear_camera/image_raw, /left_camera/image_raw — camera streams
/rgbd_camera — RGB-D camera stream
7. Important model files
Robot URDF: mobile_robot_base.urdf.xacro
Gazebo config: mobile_robot_gazebo.xacro
LiDAR sensor: lidar.xacro
IMU sensor: imu_sensor.xacro
Cameras: csi_cameras.xacro
